; A measured register is CLASSICAL from that point on, so firing a gate
; controlled on it afterwards is a POST-MEASURE GATE — Rule 6's loud-reject
; class. `railMeasuredBeforeReadPoint` asks `isPotentiallyReachable(measure,
; readPoint)` over the rail's WIRE closure (`railWireNamesBackward`, the r9e5
; round-1 F-B1R1-1 widening — the measurement may name any SSA name on the same
; physical rail), with the read point being `Pred->getTerminator()`.
;
; ITS DISCRIMINATOR IS `control_inplace_ry_rail_measure_after.ll`: the same
; program with the measurement AFTER the region ACCEPTS, because a measurement
; the control read can never follow is downstream and owns the register from
; there on.;
